A||||1||Ronen||oil leak on engine under ignition module||||5||
Z||000000||Ronen||05-11-2001||11:01 AM||||My question. Does anyone know what is under the ignition module on the engine block? The ignition module, off course, is located under the distributor cap. Right under the module on the block itself (about 2 inches under the module)fresh oil is seeping out from the engine. My Fiero is a '85 GT V6. I thought it was the oil pressure sending unit, which could have unbolted itself from the engine. But, I have read that the sending unit is next to the battery on the block, which is located opposite from where the oil is leaking. Can anyone help? Is it the knock sensor, and do they leak oil? Or, could it actually be the distributor cap area. Can this area leak oil? Please, help? I want to remove the cap and ignition to see whats there ( vision of the area is completely obstructed by these), but I am being told that I will need to take it to a mechanic to put back on.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-11-2001||11:09 AM||||There is an "O" ring on the base of the distributor that is an oil seal. Over time these leak. All that needs to be done is pull the distributor and replace the seal. It's not hard to do, But you need to be careful on pulling and replacing the distributor so that it goes back in at the same position it came out.<P>BTW ~ Welcome to the forum!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
